* July 1st - '''Luminosity Gaming''' part ways with their lineup following the expiration of their contracts. <ref name="Luminosity Gaming roster joins SK Gaming">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160627004015/http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/40/lg-sk-agree-to-settle-csgo-dispute|archivedate=2016-01-27|url=http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/40/lg-sk-agree-to-settle-csgo-dispute|title=LG & SK agree to settle CS:GO dispute|date=2016-06-24|publisher='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* July 30th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' acquires [[WinOut.net]]'s lineup consisting of [[PKL]], [[yeL]], [[destiny]], [[nak]], [[BIT]], and [[Apoka]], the latter as the team's coach. <ref name="LG acquires WinOut CSGO team">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160803190610/http://www.luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/42/lg-acquires-winout-csgo-team|archivedate=2016-08-03|url=http://www.luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/42/lg-acquires-winout-csgo-team|title=LG acquires WinOut CSGO team|date=2016-08-30|publisher='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* September 8th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' part ways with [[BIT]] and [[nak]]. <ref name="bit and nak leave">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/LG_bit1/status/773905224545165313|date=2016-09-08|title=Time decidiu continuar sem eu e o nak|trans_title=Team decided to continue without me and nak|{{Flag|br}} Portuguese|author=[[bit]]}}</ref>
* September 11th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' sign [[SHOOWTiME]] and [[shz]]. <ref name="LG:CSGO, adds SHOWTIME & SHZ!">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160915120248/http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/57/lgcsgo-adds-showtime-shz|archivedate=2016-09-15|url=http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/57/lgcsgo-adds-showtime-shz|title=LG:CSGO, adds SHOWTIME & shz!|date=2016-09-11|publisher='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>

|content3=
* January 2nd - '''Luminosity Gaming''' replace [[Apoka]] with [[felippe1]]. <ref name="felippe replaces Apoka">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170104070909/http://mycnb.uol.com.br/noticias/5108-felippe1-e-o-novo-treinador-de-counter-strike-do-luminosity|archivedate=2017-01-04|url=http://mycnb.uol.com.br/noticias/5108-felippe1-e-o-novo-treinador-de-counter-strike-do-luminosity|date=2017-01-02|title=Felippe1 é o novo treinador de Counter-Strike do Luminosity|trans_title=felippe1 is the new coach of Luminosity Counter-Strike|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|author=[[Gabriel Oliveira]]|publisher=[[MyCNB]]}}</ref>
* July 13th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' part ways with [[destiny]], [[shz]], and [[felippe1]] while adding [[chelo]] and [[NEKIZ]]. <ref name="Three out, chelo and NEKIZ in">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170716215027/http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/81/welcome-chelo-nekiz-to-lg-csgo|archivedate=2017-07-16|url=http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/gaming/81/welcome-chelo-nekiz-to-lg-csgo|date=2017-07-13|title=Welcome chelo & NEKIZ to LG CS:GO|publisher='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* August 21st - [[Apoka]] rejoins '''Luminosity Gaming'''. <ref name="Apoka back to LG">{{cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/aleapokaaa/posts/941939492625831|date=2017-08-21|title=Today I would like to officially announce that im back to Coach Luminosity's CSGO|author=[[Apoka]]}}</ref>

|content4=
* April 22nd - '''Luminosity Gaming''' replace [[chelo]] and [[Apoka]] with [[steel (Lucas Lopes)|steel]] and [[zakk]]. <ref name="two out, zakk and steel in">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Luminosity/status/988123658638970880|date=2018-04-22|title=Welcome @steelegabr & coach @IMTzakk to #LGCSGO|publisher='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* June 10th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' bench [[PKL]] and [[SHOOWTiME]] while signing [[HEN1]] and [[LUCAS1]]. <ref name="two out, two in">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180614085313/http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/general/92/lg-csgo-adds-hen1-lucas1|archivedate=2018-01-14|url=http://luminosity.gg/articles/news/general/92/lg-csgo-adds-hen1-lucas1|date=2018-06-10|title=LG CSGO adds HEN1 & LUCAS1|publisher='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* June 16th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' part ways with [[SHOOWTiME]]. <ref name="show leaves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/LG_SHOOWTiME/status/1008092757582319616|date=2018-06-16|title=I’m officially free agent and looking for a new home|author=[[SHOOWTiME]]}}</ref>
* June 26th - [[PKL]] is acquired by [[Virtue Gaming]]. <ref name="pkl joins virtue">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/VrT_Gaming/status/1011731812916318208|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|title=Chega de espera!|trans_title=No more waiting!|date=2018-06-26|author=[[Virtue Gaming]]}}</ref>
* December 12th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' replace [[yeL]] with [[boltz]]. <ref name="boltz joins LG">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Luminosity/status/1072870840088256517|title=Roster Update: Join us in welcoming @Boltz to #LGCSGO!|author='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>

|content5=
* June 25th - [[LUCAS1]] is loaned to [[MIBR]] while '''Luminosity Gaming''' acquire [[felps]] on loan from [[MIBR]]. <ref name="LUCAS1 leaves to MIBR">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/mibr/status/1143629074113318912|date=2019-06-25|title=Welcome to the MIBR family @LUCAS1!|author=[[MIBR]]}}</ref><ref name="felps loan">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Luminosity/status/1143730937668296704|date=2019-06-25|title=@felperaa will join our starting roster (on loan) and @LUCAS1 will join @mibr (on loan)|author='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* August 20th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' bench [[HEN1]]. <ref name="HEN1 benched">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Luminosity/status/1163952688280641537|date=2019-08-20|title=CS:GO Roster Update: Effective immediately @HEN1 has been moved to a the bench and is a restricted free agent. Interested parties should contact us|author='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* September 9th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' acquire [[skullz]] on loan from [[W7M Gaming]]. <ref name="skullz loan">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/n/27820|date=2019-09-09|title=Luminosity add skullz on loan|publisher=[[HLTV]]|author=[[Nohte]]}}</ref>
* September 12th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' release their lineup. <ref name="lumino released">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/27854/official-luminosity-release-roster|date=2019-09-12|title=Official: Luminosity release roster|publisher=[[HLTV]]|author=[[Professeur]]}}</ref><ref name="lucas1 free transfer to MIBR">{{inside source}}</ref>

|content6=
* July 1st - '''Luminosity Gaming''' announce their entry into ''[[Counter-Strike 2]]'' by acquiring [[Rainwaker]] from [[Monte]] and signing [[afro]], [[AZUWU]], [[Bymas]], and [[lux]]. <ref name="cs2">{{cite web|url=https://luminosity-0b85b1.webflow.io/news/lg-returns-to-counter-strike|title=LG RETURNS TO COUNTER STRIKE!|date=2026-07-01|publisher='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* August 24th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' bench [[Bymas]]. <ref name="Bymas bench">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Luminosity/status/2091973468510150868|date=2026-08-24|title=ROSTER UPDATE|author='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* August 25th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' acquire [[kakafu]] and [[yxngstxr]] from [[Monte]] and [[HEROIC]], respectively, the former as their new coach. <ref name="+kakafu">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/luminosity/status/2092238655800684953|date=2026-08-25|title=Finally official|author='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref><ref name="+yxngstxr">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Luminosity/status/2092270134605848680|date=2026-08-25|title=Welcome the official team yapper|author='''Luminosity Gaming'''}}</ref>
* October 6th - '''Luminosity Gaming''' release [[Bymas]]. <ref name="-Bymas">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/bymascs/status/2107434935694836221|title=As of today, I’m a free agent and open to offers|date=2026-10-06|author=[[Bymas]]}}</ref>
}}

